 `CustomerRepository` deliberately behaves like a real paged backend: it refuses
 to return more than `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (200) rows in a single call. Callers page.
+Filtering, sorting and counting all happen in the repository, so the grid only
+ever holds one page of rows.
+
+## Filtering
+
+The view at `/` filters by name and by status. A customer is shown when it
+matches both:
+
+- **Name:** the text is split on whitespace, and every term must appear in the
+  first or the last name, ignoring case and accents.
+- **Status:** with none selected, every status matches.
+
+The filter is kept in the address, so a narrowed list can be bookmarked or sent
+on: `/?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`. An empty filter leaves no parameters.

